  "notes": "Huawei figures for the F1A-C (CR8B0BKP03E0): 56 physical ports maximum, 8x100GE, 20x25GE, 48x10GE, 28xGE/FE electrical-capable SFP slots, 2.4 Tbit/s switching, 336.3 W typical (1091.1 BTU/h), 1U 43.6 x 442 x 420 mm, 7 kg, AC 100-240 V / 240 V HVDC, 1+1 power, 3+1 fans. It is the same 56-position panel as the F1A-8H20Q but a narrower port map: the 25GE range is one unbroken 28-47 block with no 1GE mode, and the datasheet states breakout \"No\", interface rate auto-sensing \"No\", FlexE \"No\", MACsec \"No\" - so unlike the 8H20Q it cannot split a 100GE port into 4x25GE. Marketing datasheet gives the same 1.2 Tbit/s \"maximum port capacity\" while the hardware description states 2.4 Tbit/s switching capacity. Management ports (MGMT-ETH RJ45, Console/AUX RJ45, TOD, CLK, USB, reserved GE0/GE1 SFP) are not modelled. https://support.huawei.com/enterprise/en/doc/EDOC1100465707/7044fd1d/netengine-8000-f1a-c",
  "sourceUrl": "https://support.huawei.com/enterprise/en/doc/EDOC1100465707/7044fd1d/netengine-8000-f1a-c",
